{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nCloud/DC atomic executors need a core route that bypasses generic retry without falsely advancing the current handler baseline. Production must remain on legacy until S3 validates and cuts over.\n\n## Outcome\nAdd a constructor-injected legacy-default selector for exact summary updates, map confirmed outcomes through the existing result surface, and expose terminal outcomes as bounded per-mutation errors without baseline/provenance advance. Finalize the S1 section of ADR 0103.\n\n## Plan\n1. Route only exact `{\"summary\"}` when tests explicitly enable the selector. Mixed fields remain one unsplit legacy call. Add no config/env key and never dual-send.\n2. Poison-test generic `_call_with_retry` on the selected route. Preserve every unselected route.\n3. Map the three SUCCESS dispositions the summary executors can return — `applied`, `recovered`, `already_satisfied` — to the legacy result surface (`_fields_synced`, `_comment_errors`, `_subop` shapes) and advance the ADR-0026 baseline. These three, and only these three, are the success cohort.\n4. Map EVERY other disposition the summary executors can return — `commit_unknown`, `retryable_deferred`, `exhausted_transient`, `permanent_failure`, and any further non-success disposition (`dependency_deferred`, `scope_deferred`, `safety_aborted`, `skipped`) — identically as TERMINAL: emit an internal tagged result consumed by `handle_update` that records exactly one redacted per-mutation error/disposition message capped at 512 Unicode code points, carries the OperationOutcome `retry_not_before` value (a RetryPlan field, not a disposition) for observability only, keeps `_fields_synced` empty, advances no baseline/provenance, persists no S1 deferral, and continues the batch.\n5. Name S3 as sole cutover, fuse/deferral consumer, and bridge-retirement owner in contract/ADR.\n\n## Testing\nUse exact-versus-mixed routing tables, poison retries, Cloud/DC verified fakes, and apply-handler spies asserting one message, redaction, the 512-code-point boundary, baseline, and provenance across both the success cohort and the terminal cohort.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The internal selector defaults to legacy and adds no config or environment key.\n- [ ] Test-enabled exact summary bypasses generic retry, while mixed fields remain one legacy call.\n- [ ] The three success dispositions (`applied`, `recovered`, `already_satisfied`) preserve all existing result and telemetry shapes and advance the baseline.\n- [ ] Every non-success disposition (`commit_unknown`, `retryable_deferred`, `exhausted_transient`, `permanent_failure`, and any further terminal disposition) records exactly one redacted per-mutation error/disposition message capped at 512 Unicode code points and never advances baseline or provenance.\n- [ ] Terminal outcomes persist no deferral in S1 and do not stop unrelated batch work.\n- [ ] ADR 0103 names S3 as sole production cutover, fuse/deferral consumer, and compatibility-bridge retirement owner.\n\n## Out of scope\nDefault-on routing, fuse behavior, and durable deferral remain RP-03 S3."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787580737245869001,"uuid":"9db2dc85-d8fe-4ecc-877f-be86e08eaa36"}